IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `oas-core`
IMPORT `oas-core-measures`

-- Old Age Security Regulations (C.R.C., c. 1246): the short title (regulation 1, which says nothing to compute) and the Interpretation
-- section (regulation 2): the definitions of regulation 2(1), residence and presence in Newfoundland before union (2(2)) and the
-- "prescribed individual" for the Act's definition of "public officer" (2(3)).
--
-- A definition is encoded as a rule that says when the defined thing is what the Regulations say it is. Where the Regulations only
-- give a defined word a name ("Act" for the Old Age Security Act, "Court" for the Tax Court of Canada) the rule is the identity on a
-- fact the person states, so that the word can be called by name and its definition stays beside its source line. The repealed
-- definitions are recorded in NOTES.md and encoded nowhere.

§ `Short Title`

-- Regulation 1: "These Regulations may be cited as the Old Age Security Regulations." It is a title, not a rule.
-- src:11 | 1 These Regulations may be cited as the Old Age Security Regulations.
-- (no rule: nothing in the Regulations depends on the title)

§ `Interpretation`

§§ `Definitions (regulation 2(1))`

-- src:15 | Act means the Old Age Security Act; (Loi)
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 2(1) "Act" (src:15)
GIVEN `the statute is the Old Age Security Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 2(1): the statute is the Act` `the statute is the Old Age Security Act` MEANS
    `the statute is the Old Age Security Act`

-- src:16 | appeal means an appeal referred to in subsection 28(1) of the Act or made in respect of a reference; (appel)
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 2(1) "appeal" (src:16)
GIVEN `the appeal is an appeal referred to in subsection 28(1) of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appeal is made in respect of a reference` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 2(1): the appeal is an appeal for the purposes of these Regulations` `the appeal is an appeal referred to in subsection 28(1) of the Act` `the appeal is made in respect of a reference` MEANS
        `the appeal is an appeal referred to in subsection 28(1) of the Act`
    OR  `the appeal is made in respect of a reference`

-- src:17 | appellant means a person who makes an appeal referred to in subsection 28(1) or (2) of the Act or in respect of a reference; (appelant)
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 2(1) "appellant" (src:17)
GIVEN `the person makes an appeal referred to in subsection 28(1) or (2) of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person makes an appeal in respect of a reference` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 2(1): the person is an appellant` `the person makes an appeal referred to in subsection 28(1) or (2) of the Act` `the person makes an appeal in respect of a reference` MEANS
        `the person makes an appeal referred to in subsection 28(1) or (2) of the Act`
    OR  `the person makes an appeal in respect of a reference`

-- src:19 | application form means the form of application required by the Minister; (formule de demande)
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 2(1) "application form" (src:19)
GIVEN `the form is the form of application required by the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 2(1): the form is an application form` `the form is the form of application required by the Minister` MEANS
    `the form is the form of application required by the Minister`

-- src:20 | beneficiary includes a person on whose behalf a benefit has become payable; (prestataire)
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 2(1) "beneficiary" (src:20)
GIVEN `the person is a beneficiary within the meaning of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a benefit has become payable on behalf of the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 2(1): the person is a beneficiary for the purposes of these Regulations` `the person is a beneficiary within the meaning of the Act` `a benefit has become payable on behalf of the person` MEANS
        `the person is a beneficiary within the meaning of the Act`
    OR  `a benefit has become payable on behalf of the person`

-- src:22 | Court means the Tax Court of Canada constituted by the Tax Court of Canada Act; (Cour)
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 2(1) "Court" (src:22)
GIVEN `the court is the Tax Court of Canada constituted by the Tax Court of Canada Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 2(1): the court is the Court` `the court is the Tax Court of Canada constituted by the Tax Court of Canada Act` MEANS
