§§ `Newfoundland (regulation 2(2))`

-- 2(2): residence and presence in Newfoundland BEFORE the date of union of Newfoundland with Canada are deemed to be residence and
-- presence in Canada. The Regulations do not state the date of union; it arrives as an input (31 March 1949 is the date the
-- Newfoundland Act gives, which is outside the text this piece encodes). "Prior to" excludes the day of union itself, on which the
-- person was in Canada in fact.
-- src:31 | (2) For the purposes of these Regulations, residence and presence in Newfoundland prior to the date of union of Newfoundland with Canada are deemed to be residence and presence in Canada respectively.
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 2(2) (src:31)
GIVEN `the day on which the person resided or was present in Newfoundland` IS A DATE
      `the date of union of Newfoundland with Canada` IS A DATE -- out of range: the Newfoundland Act (the Regulations name the date and do not state it)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 2(2): the residence or presence in Newfoundland on the day is deemed to be residence or presence in Canada` `the day on which the person resided or was present in Newfoundland` `the date of union of Newfoundland with Canada` MEANS
    `the day on which the person resided or was present in Newfoundland` LESS THAN `the date of union of Newfoundland with Canada`

§§ `Public officer (regulation 2(3))`

-- 2(3): for the Act's definition of "public officer" in section 33(1), a prescribed individual is a person employed in a federal
-- institution or whose services are required by one, on a casual or temporary basis or under a student employment program. The
-- encoding reads the closing words as qualifying both kinds of person (fork F-2(3) in NOTES.md).
-- src:32 | (3) For the purpose of the definition public officer in subsection 33(1) of the Act, a prescribed individual is a person employed in a federal institution or whose services are required by a federal institution, on a casual or temporary basis or under a student employment program.
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 2(3) (src:32)
GIVEN `the person is employed in a federal institution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person's services are required by a federal institution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is so employed or engaged on a casual or temporary basis` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is so employed or engaged under a student employment program` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 2(3): the individual is a prescribed individual for the purpose of the definition public officer in subsection 33(1) of the Act` `the person is employed in a federal institution` `the person's services are required by a federal institution` `the person is so employed or engaged on a casual or temporary basis` `the person is so employed or engaged under a student employment program` MEANS
        (   `the person is employed in a federal institution`
         OR `the person's services are required by a federal institution`)
    AND (   `the person is so employed or engaged on a casual or temporary basis`
         OR `the person is so employed or engaged under a student employment program`)
